! Getting Started with Legal Wiki

This guide will help you set up and start using Legal Wiki for your legal practice.

!! Understanding the Structure

Legal Wiki uses a tag-based organization system:

|!Tag |!Purpose |
|`Case` |Active legal cases |
|`Client` |Client information records |
|`Research` |Legal research notes and citations |
|`Template` |Reusable document templates |
|`Deadline` |Important dates and deadlines |
|`Statute` |Statutory references |
|`CaseLaw` |Case law citations |

!! Creating Your First Case

# Click the {{$:/core/ui/Buttons/new-tiddler}} button to create a new tiddler
# Title it with your case name (e.g., "Smith v. Jones")
# Add the `Case` tag
# Use the [[New Case Template]] as a starting point

!! Organizing Research

For legal research, create tiddlers with:

* Clear, descriptive titles
* Appropriate tags (`Research`, `Statute`, `CaseLaw`)
* Links to related cases and documents
* Citations in a consistent format

!! Using Templates

Templates are pre-formatted tiddlers you can copy:

* [[New Case Template]] - Start a new case file
* [[Client Intake Template]] - Record new client information
* [[Legal Memo Template]] - Draft legal memoranda
* [[Deadline Tracker Template]] - Track important dates

!! Best Practices

* ''Consistent Naming'' - Use a standard naming convention for cases
* ''Regular Backups'' - Save and backup your wiki regularly
* ''Tag Everything'' - Tags make finding information much easier
* ''Link Liberally'' - Create connections between related content
* ''Date Your Entries'' - Include dates on research notes and updates
